My first wishless ascension!

Biggest problem -- no bag. At all. Not even a sack. Until I already
had the amulet, and was running up through Gehennom. On one of the
many mysterious force throwbacks, I happened across a mummy who had
left a bag of holding, so I was able to carry stuff up to the Planes,
but until then, I just had to keep teleporting back and forth to the
stash/temple on level 18.

Less of a problem -- lowly enchanted armor. Came across 1 magic marker
the entire game, and it was almost empty, so I got a couple ID's out
of it, then recharged it and got my speed boots repaired and up to +5.

I did have a lot of divine protection though, more than I usually do.

I extincted soldiers -- my first 'real' extinction (so, something
that's not erinyes).

Got 6 of the Nazgul. Grr. I swear, sometime I'm just going to reverse
genocide them so I can get them all.

I had no MR for much of the early game, at least until the castle.
Couldn't beat Ixoth without MR, so I ran away and left him alone.
Finally ID'd a genocide scroll, and reverse genocided grey dragons.
One of them left scales, which I wore until I ID'd enchant armor and I
could turn it into mail. Once I had MR, Ixoth died pretty quickly.

Polyselfed into a silver dragon to lay a few eggs. The two twins that
hatched, San Marco and San Polo, followed me around until San Polo
grew up, and San Marco was killed in action. I rode San Polo for quite
a long time, before a minotaur got him. Didn't ride a steed after
that, as cool as it is. (My starting horse, Castello, died pretty
quickly. I had another horse, Cannaregio, but he died fairly quickly
as well. Horses suck.)

I guess that's about it.

I've gotten Val/Bar/Sam/Hea/Arc/Mon/Wiz, and now Kni. It's funny,
after I ascended my first character, the Valkyrie, I always thought
I'd do Priest next. *still* haven't gotten a priest.. I think I got to
the quest once, but not sure.

And now that I've done wishless, that's as much conduct as I'm
probably going to get... I can't ever see myself getting, say, athiest
or illiterate. Maybe I'll try. I never got Vegitarian (I messed up
with the monk -- she ate a stupid black pudding), that might be
possible.


